{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Cancel Effects","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every effect the store runs is already cancelled on teardown: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()"},{"type":"text","text":" and the store’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":" cancel all in-flight effect tasks. That is enough for cleanup, but it is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"all-or-nothing","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — you cannot cancel one specific effect while others keep running."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keyed cancellation adds that. You give an effect a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"cancel id","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and later cancel every effect running under that id with the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)"},{"type":"text","text":" effect or the imperative "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method. Identity lives outside the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect"},{"type":"text","text":" type — it is still a plain closure — so nothing about reducer signatures changes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reach for this when an effect outlives the action that started it: cancelling text-to-speech when the user skips, debouncing a search field, or tearing down a long-lived listener when a screen disappears."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Choosing an id","anchor":"Choosing-an-id","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A cancel id is any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable & Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" value. Distinct ids are independent; effects sharing an id are cancelled together. A dedicated empty type reads well and can’t collide with another feature’s id:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["private enum SearchID: Hashable, Sendable {}","private enum SpeechID: Hashable, Sendable {}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Strings and enums work too — pick whatever is unambiguous in your domain."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Cancel from inside a reducer","anchor":"Cancel-from-inside-a-reducer","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Return "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to tag the work, and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to stop it:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["case .startSpeaking(let text):","    return cancellable(id: SpeechID()) { send in","        for await word in speech.speak(text) {","            await send(.spokeWord(word))","        }","    }","","case .skip:","    \/\/ Stop any in-flight speech immediately.","    return cancel(id: SpeechID())"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the speaking effect is cancelled, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for await"},{"type":"text","text":" loop ends at the next suspension point, exactly as it would on teardown."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Debounce with `cancelInFlight`","anchor":"Debounce-with-cancelInFlight","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Passing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cancelInFlight: true"},{"type":"text","text":" cancels any effect already running under the id "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" starting the new one — the whole of debounce in one line:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["case .queryChanged(let query):","    return cancellable(id: SearchID(), cancelInFlight: true) { send in","        try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(300))","        let results = try await api.search(query)","        await send(.results(results))","    }"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each keystroke re-dispatches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".queryChanged"},{"type":"text","text":"; the new effect cancels the previous sleeping one, so only the last query in a burst reaches the network."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Cancel from view or scene code","anchor":"Cancel-from-view-or-scene-code","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When there is no reducer action to hang the cancellation on — a screen disappearing, a sheet dismissing — call "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)"},{"type":"text","text":" directly:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":[".onDisappear {","    store.cancel(id: SearchID())","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ids with nothing running are ignored, so it is always safe to call."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"What it does not replace","anchor":"What-it-does-not-replace","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keyed cancellation is not a substitute for resource cleanup. An effect holding a file handle, a network connection, or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream"},{"type":"text","text":" continuation should still release it — use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withTaskCancellationHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" or a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"defer"},{"type":"text","text":". Cancellation ends the task; it does not close what the task opened."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effects that terminate on their own (a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for await"},{"type":"text","text":" loop whose stream finishes) need no id at all. Only reach for a cancel id when something "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"else","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" has to stop the effect early."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"],"generated":true,"anchor":"How-to-Guides","title":"How-to Guides"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Tag an effect with an identity so it can be cancelled later — by another effect, or imperatively from view code.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtocanceleffects"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Tags an effect with a cancellation identity so it can later be cancelled by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.cancel(id:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cancellable","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"},{"text":" & ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cancelInFlight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux6Effecta","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux6Effecta"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelinflight:_:)"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/cancel(id:)":{"title":"cancel(id:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cancel"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"},{"text":" & ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s: